1
00:00:15,120 --> 00:00:17,280
Our company just landed a major project

2
00:00:17,280 --> 00:00:18,560
worth tens of millions.

3
00:00:18,560 --> 00:00:21,640
So I’ll let Dan and Saint handle the project.

4
00:00:21,640 --> 00:00:23,160
Uh, Dan. Could you—

5
00:00:23,160 --> 00:00:24,040
Sorry.

6
00:00:24,040 --> 00:00:25,720
I don’t work outside office hours.

7
00:00:25,720 --> 00:00:26,720
Six o’clock sharp.

8
00:00:26,720 --> 00:00:27,920
Leave on time.

9
00:00:27,920 --> 00:00:28,720
Just you wait.

10
00:00:28,720 --> 00:00:30,720
I’m taking him down.

11
00:00:30,720 --> 00:00:32,360
SaintDan! SaintDan! SaintDan!

12
00:00:32,360 --> 00:00:33,520
Stop!

13
00:00:35,880 --> 00:00:36,960
I like…

14
00:00:36,960 --> 00:00:38,280
Don’t be afraid, Dan.

15
00:00:38,640 --> 00:00:41,280
I won’t let Kimhan do anything to my little brother.

16
00:00:51,240 --> 00:00:53,000
What I fear most in life…

17
00:00:53,440 --> 00:00:54,680
isn’t failure.

18
00:00:55,240 --> 00:00:56,920
It’s having the secret

19
00:00:56,920 --> 00:00:59,720
I’ve spent my whole life hiding

20
00:01:00,200 --> 00:01:01,600
getting exposed.

21
00:01:48,320 --> 00:01:51,160
And the person who holds most of my secret

22
00:01:51,440 --> 00:01:52,600
is…

23
00:01:52,840 --> 00:01:54,479
Good morning, Mr. Kimhan.

24
00:01:55,600 --> 00:01:56,880
Today you have a meeting

25
00:01:56,880 --> 00:01:59,160
about Siam Central Luxury Mall.

26
00:02:22,320 --> 00:02:23,640
Let’s get started.

27
00:03:46,240 --> 00:03:48,320
Uncle Kim!

28
00:03:49,240 --> 00:03:50,240
Yes?

29
00:03:50,680 --> 00:03:51,640
Hm?

30
00:03:52,680 --> 00:03:55,400
Why didn’t you tell me you were back?

31
00:03:55,400 --> 00:03:57,920
How long are you staying in Bangkok?

32
00:03:57,920 --> 00:03:59,640
Don’t go back to America, okay?.

33
00:03:59,640 --> 00:04:02,480
I want to play with you every day.

34
00:04:02,600 --> 00:04:04,040
Of course.

35
00:04:04,280 --> 00:04:06,920
Uncle will play with Gina every day.

36
00:04:07,080 --> 00:04:10,720
Can we get ice cream at our usual place?

37
00:04:11,800 --> 00:04:13,040
Okay.

38
00:04:13,560 --> 00:04:15,760
Pinky promise?

39
00:04:22,680 --> 00:04:23,440
Yay!

40
00:04:23,440 --> 00:04:25,440
You promised!

41
00:04:25,440 --> 00:04:30,680
I’ll dress up pretty and see you every day.

42
00:04:30,680 --> 00:04:31,960
Okay.

43
00:04:31,960 --> 00:04:33,200
See you.

44
00:04:45,800 --> 00:04:47,840
This time, I’m not going anywhere.

45
00:04:52,520 --> 00:04:53,600
So…

46
00:04:53,600 --> 00:04:55,080
About yesterday…

47
00:04:55,080 --> 00:04:56,840
I’m really sorry, Dan.

48
00:04:58,040 --> 00:04:59,080
Is it too lame?

49
00:04:59,080 --> 00:05:00,880
Dan, I’m sorry.

50
00:05:00,880 --> 00:05:02,880
Too casual?

51
00:05:02,880 --> 00:05:05,560
Dan, I really feel bad.

52
00:05:05,840 --> 00:05:09,040
I was too harsh.

53
00:05:09,320 --> 00:05:10,360
That won’t work.

54
00:05:11,360 --> 00:05:15,360
I’m sorry about what I said yesterday.

55
00:05:16,040 --> 00:05:17,800
I was too harsh.

56
00:05:17,800 --> 00:05:19,040
Will it take much longer?

57
00:05:20,280 --> 00:05:21,760
If it’ll take a while,

58
00:05:22,360 --> 00:05:23,600
let me put my bag down first.

59
00:05:27,680 --> 00:05:29,000
About yesterday,

60
00:05:30,280 --> 00:05:31,520
I’m sorry.

61
00:05:31,880 --> 00:05:33,280
I was too harsh.

62
00:05:33,760 --> 00:05:36,280
And I judged you without knowing you,

63
00:05:38,040 --> 00:05:42,240
or trying to talk thing through with you.

64
00:05:42,480 --> 00:05:43,640
I’m used to it.

65
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:47,240
Everyone judges me by how I look.

66
00:05:51,720 --> 00:05:52,920
My bag.

67
00:05:52,920 --> 00:05:54,040
My clothes.

68
00:05:55,120 --> 00:05:56,280
My looks.

69
00:05:57,400 --> 00:05:58,400
And my car.

70
00:06:00,240 --> 00:06:01,400
Those things

71
00:06:01,920 --> 00:06:03,880
are easier to judge someone by

72
00:06:04,600 --> 00:06:06,920
than asking what they do,

73
00:06:08,200 --> 00:06:09,520
how they work,

74
00:06:10,440 --> 00:06:11,480
or what’s on their mind.

75
00:06:12,920 --> 00:06:14,880
Then can I ask you now?

76
00:06:16,400 --> 00:06:17,280
About what?

77
00:06:17,440 --> 00:06:19,040
How you work,

78
00:06:19,760 --> 00:06:22,040
and how you think.

79
00:06:22,320 --> 00:06:22,960
Oh.

80
00:06:23,160 --> 00:06:26,320
Let me buy you a coffee to make up for it.

81
00:06:36,040 --> 00:06:38,840
I’ve wanted to apologize since last night.

82
00:06:40,800 --> 00:06:42,040
I know.

83
00:06:44,600 --> 00:06:45,840
But just so you know,

84
00:06:46,520 --> 00:06:48,560
I’m pretty picky about coffee.

85
00:06:51,120 --> 00:06:53,000
That figures.

86
00:06:53,920 --> 00:06:54,720
Hey!

87
00:06:55,480 --> 00:06:57,280
You just apologized to me, remember?

88
00:07:01,040 --> 00:07:01,880
Yes.

89
00:07:02,600 --> 00:07:06,600
I’m trying to fix my bad habits.

90
00:07:10,600 --> 00:07:11,920
I’d like to order, please.

91
00:07:11,920 --> 00:07:14,640
A double-shot frappe latte

92
00:07:14,640 --> 00:07:17,160
with oat milk and whipped cream,

93
00:07:17,160 --> 00:07:19,520
drizzled with caramel and chocolate sauce,

94
00:07:19,520 --> 00:07:22,040
and extra almonds, please.

95
00:07:22,440 --> 00:07:24,280
-Sure.
-Thank you.

96
00:07:26,400 --> 00:07:27,480
And I'll have...

97
00:07:27,880 --> 00:07:29,320
an iced Americano.

98
00:07:29,720 --> 00:07:32,360
Sure, that’ll be 375 baht.

99
00:07:37,640 --> 00:07:39,400
-Just a moment, please.
-Thank you.

100
00:07:43,480 --> 00:07:44,760
Thanks for the coffee.

101
00:07:45,720 --> 00:07:47,080
Then I guess...

102
00:07:47,720 --> 00:07:49,159
we’re even.

103
00:07:51,240 --> 00:07:52,760
I’ve been thinking about it.

104
00:07:53,600 --> 00:07:55,320
This project means a lot to me.

105
00:07:55,880 --> 00:07:57,080
It’s a big project,

106
00:07:58,040 --> 00:08:00,240
and my chance to prove myself.

107
00:08:02,720 --> 00:08:04,400
I really want to do well.

108
00:08:04,760 --> 00:08:06,840
It means a lot to me too.

109
00:08:08,200 --> 00:08:09,320
Actually, at first,

110
00:08:09,600 --> 00:08:12,240
I even asked P’Ta to take me off this project.

111
00:08:13,200 --> 00:08:14,680
But she said

112
00:08:15,160 --> 00:08:16,960
the client specifically requested

113
00:08:16,960 --> 00:08:19,400
a top-selling AE like me.

114
00:08:21,320 --> 00:08:22,600
At least

115
00:08:23,120 --> 00:08:24,440
I get an opportunity

116
00:08:24,880 --> 00:08:27,080
to work with someone as good as you.

117
00:08:28,840 --> 00:08:31,240
Well, we’re stuck with each other.

118
00:08:32,880 --> 00:08:34,360
How about this?

119
00:08:35,400 --> 00:08:37,480
Let’s try to be good teammates.

120
00:08:40,919 --> 00:08:41,720
Deal?

121
00:08:47,720 --> 00:08:48,600
Deal.

122
00:08:59,080 --> 00:09:00,200
What’s with that look?

123
00:09:01,800 --> 00:09:02,920
We agreed

124
00:09:03,120 --> 00:09:04,720
to be good teammates, remember?

125
00:09:06,360 --> 00:09:07,800
Would a good teammate...

126
00:09:07,800 --> 00:09:10,440
dump this mountain of files on me?

127
00:09:10,440 --> 00:09:12,040
A good teammate

128
00:09:12,720 --> 00:09:14,720
just wants you to be prepared

129
00:09:14,720 --> 00:09:15,920
before the actual meeting.

130
00:09:19,880 --> 00:09:20,920
Good luck.

131
00:09:20,920 --> 00:09:21,880
Bye.

132
00:09:27,280 --> 00:09:30,040
What’s with him?

133
00:09:36,400 --> 00:09:37,360
Tomorrow,

134
00:09:38,040 --> 00:09:40,240
I’m taking down the top-selling AE.

135
00:09:41,720 --> 00:09:42,880
Just you wait.

136
00:09:43,920 --> 00:09:44,720
Ugh!

137
00:10:05,760 --> 00:10:08,200
Am I working or taking the bar exam?

138
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:19,920
Ah!

139
00:10:22,360 --> 00:10:23,520
I thought you were a ghost.

140
00:10:24,800 --> 00:10:25,680
Dan.

141
00:10:26,840 --> 00:10:27,560
Here.

142
00:10:28,200 --> 00:10:29,600
I brought you some food

143
00:10:30,040 --> 00:10:33,080
to help you fight that mountain of paperwork.

144
00:10:33,480 --> 00:10:34,920
Easy now.

145
00:10:36,840 --> 00:10:37,760
Thank you.

146
00:10:39,640 --> 00:10:41,160
I’m not being nice.

147
00:10:41,840 --> 00:10:44,040
I’m just worried you won’t survive long enough

148
00:10:44,040 --> 00:10:45,640
to submit the work tomorrow.

149
00:10:47,560 --> 00:10:50,200
I thought I’d have to go on a ghost-hunting show.

150
00:11:13,960 --> 00:11:15,400
Uh…

151
00:11:18,120 --> 00:11:19,000
Here.

152
00:11:19,960 --> 00:11:20,520
Right here.

153
00:11:25,880 --> 00:11:26,640
What is it?

154
00:11:52,960 --> 00:11:54,200
Cilantro.

155
00:11:55,160 --> 00:11:57,000
You’ve got cilantro there.

156
00:11:57,160 --> 00:11:58,240
Thank you.

157
00:11:59,200 --> 00:12:00,440
It was starting to annoy me.

158
00:12:09,320 --> 00:12:10,800
I wanna go home already!

159
00:12:14,120 --> 00:12:15,320
You can't.

160
00:12:15,840 --> 00:12:16,880
We’re not done yet.

161
00:12:22,640 --> 00:12:23,880
And it’s due tomorrow.

162
00:12:28,080 --> 00:12:29,400
Then…

163
00:12:31,320 --> 00:12:33,000
Would you like to come work at my condo?

164
00:12:40,800 --> 00:12:41,960
This way.

165
00:12:53,840 --> 00:12:54,800
So…

166
00:12:55,080 --> 00:12:56,400
Where are we working?

167
00:12:56,840 --> 00:12:57,640
Over there.

168
00:13:02,720 --> 00:13:03,360
Sorry.

169
00:13:03,880 --> 00:13:06,280
My place is a bit small.

170
00:13:07,120 --> 00:13:09,200
It’s fine. The lighting’s just right.

171
00:13:15,160 --> 00:13:16,680
Take your time.

172
00:13:16,680 --> 00:13:18,160
I don’t mind.

173
00:13:33,080 --> 00:13:34,080
Here’s some water.

174
00:13:34,280 --> 00:13:35,280
Thanks.

175
00:13:46,360 --> 00:13:47,000
So…

176
00:13:47,960 --> 00:13:49,400
Where do I start?

177
00:13:50,080 --> 00:13:51,280
How far have you gotten?

178
00:13:51,960 --> 00:13:52,920
Let me see.

179
00:14:02,960 --> 00:14:03,680
Here.

180
00:14:04,440 --> 00:14:08,920
These are the visitor traffic figures for Siam Central.

181
00:14:09,200 --> 00:14:10,160
Well…

182
00:14:10,600 --> 00:14:15,200
High foot traffic doesn’t necessarily mean high sales.

183
00:14:17,000 --> 00:14:19,880
You need to find more sales data.

184
00:14:22,440 --> 00:14:23,280
Oh.

185
00:14:23,520 --> 00:14:24,240
Right.

186
00:14:24,600 --> 00:14:25,800
More research.

187
00:14:27,920 --> 00:14:29,520
Where did this figure come from?

188
00:14:30,360 --> 00:14:31,440
This one?

189
00:14:31,440 --> 00:14:34,720
It’s an estimate of Central’s customers’

190
00:14:34,720 --> 00:14:36,280
purchasing power.

191
00:14:37,600 --> 00:14:40,600
I’ll send you the file.

192
00:14:40,840 --> 00:14:42,720
It’ll give you a better idea.

193
00:14:52,080 --> 00:14:53,440
You’re more hardworking than I expected.

194
00:14:56,160 --> 00:14:59,240
I don’t want to look unprofessional.

195
00:15:00,800 --> 00:15:02,120
Then take a break.

196
00:15:02,120 --> 00:15:03,400
We still have plenty of time.

197
00:15:05,160 --> 00:15:07,640
Then you’ll dump another pile of files on me tomorrow.

198
00:15:08,960 --> 00:15:12,560
That depends on how hard you work tonight.

199
00:15:22,520 --> 00:15:23,120
Water.

200
00:15:25,320 --> 00:15:26,520
Let me refill it for you.

201
00:15:28,320 --> 00:15:28,640
Sure.

202
00:15:45,520 --> 00:15:46,640
Here you go.

203
00:15:47,840 --> 00:15:49,240
-Thank you.
-You’re welcome.

204
00:16:03,360 --> 00:16:04,040
Hey.

205
00:16:04,800 --> 00:16:06,120
Are you okay?

206
00:16:06,720 --> 00:16:07,960
I’m fine.

207
00:16:09,080 --> 00:16:10,520
Never better.

208
00:16:12,000 --> 00:16:13,320
Why don’t you turn down the AC?

209
00:16:13,640 --> 00:16:15,160
You’re sweating.

210
00:16:18,960 --> 00:16:20,680
I get hot easily.

211
00:16:21,120 --> 00:16:22,520
I can tell.

212
00:16:22,960 --> 00:16:24,400
You turned down the AC at the office,

213
00:16:24,400 --> 00:16:25,880
and I was freezing.

214
00:16:28,840 --> 00:16:29,600
I just…

215
00:16:30,040 --> 00:16:31,440
don’t like being hot.

216
00:16:40,520 --> 00:16:41,160
Huh?

217
00:16:41,720 --> 00:16:42,360
Yeah?

218
00:16:44,520 --> 00:16:46,360
I’m gonna take a shower.

219
00:16:47,280 --> 00:16:47,880
A shower…

220
00:16:48,880 --> 00:16:49,680
might help me

221
00:16:50,520 --> 00:16:52,000
cool off a bit.

222
00:16:58,880 --> 00:17:00,080
He really gets hot easily.

223
00:19:40,760 --> 00:19:41,320
Hey!

224
00:19:41,760 --> 00:19:42,520
How’s it going?

225
00:19:43,040 --> 00:19:46,120
Burning the midnight oil with Prince Dan?

226
00:19:50,040 --> 00:19:50,840
How was it?

227
00:19:51,320 --> 00:19:53,120
Heavenly, huh?

228
00:19:53,560 --> 00:19:54,680
As if.

229
00:19:55,640 --> 00:19:57,720
And we didn’t work all night.

230
00:19:58,040 --> 00:19:59,880
What the heck?

231
00:20:00,600 --> 00:20:03,440
I thought you’d be exploding by now.

232
00:20:04,520 --> 00:20:06,680
Come on, let me see your face.

233
00:20:07,360 --> 00:20:11,280
So you actually survived Dan’s standards?

234
00:20:14,800 --> 00:20:15,720
Great!

235
00:20:16,200 --> 00:20:18,200
You passed Prince Dan’s probation test.

236
00:20:20,880 --> 00:20:23,720
How’s it working with him?

237
00:20:25,280 --> 00:20:26,120
Pretty good.

238
00:20:27,160 --> 00:20:28,520
Dan’s really talented.

239
00:20:29,800 --> 00:20:30,960
I put in the numbers,

240
00:20:30,960 --> 00:20:32,200
and Dan finds the insights.

241
00:20:32,960 --> 00:20:34,400
He’s so detail-oriented.

242
00:20:35,040 --> 00:20:37,520
Honestly, he’s more precise than AI.

243
00:20:40,280 --> 00:20:41,520
He keeps praising him.

244
00:20:41,880 --> 00:20:43,960
He isn't falling, right?

245
00:20:45,440 --> 00:20:47,040
I’m just appreciating his work.

246
00:20:49,160 --> 00:20:50,280
Looking good.

247
00:20:52,520 --> 00:20:52,920
Hey.

248
00:20:53,680 --> 00:20:54,120
Hey.

249
00:21:04,520 --> 00:21:05,960
Why don’t you let your hair down?

250
00:21:07,760 --> 00:21:09,200
It might look good.

251
00:21:14,360 --> 00:21:15,320
Like this.

252
00:21:34,520 --> 00:21:35,640
Much more handsome.

253
00:21:38,680 --> 00:21:39,440
Thank you.

254
00:21:40,320 --> 00:21:41,080
No problem.

255
00:21:41,200 --> 00:21:45,120
Just a little help from your mentor.

256
00:21:54,280 --> 00:21:56,840
Hold on. Let me gossip first.

257
00:21:57,720 --> 00:22:00,040
What’s the rush? Come join us.

258
00:22:03,560 --> 00:22:03,960
So...

259
00:22:04,160 --> 00:22:06,640
Our analysis of the target audience shows that

260
00:22:07,160 --> 00:22:08,800
interest in luxury lifestyles

261
00:22:08,800 --> 00:22:11,240
rose by 18% in Q3.

262
00:22:11,240 --> 00:22:13,760
How confident are you that it’ll exceed 18%?

263
00:22:14,480 --> 00:22:15,480
Very confident.

264
00:22:15,480 --> 00:22:17,720
We reviewed the Q1 and Q2 figures,

265
00:22:18,000 --> 00:22:19,480
and it shows steady growth.

266
00:22:20,000 --> 00:22:21,440
Our key message is

267
00:22:21,440 --> 00:22:24,280
‘Living above the ordinary’,

268
00:22:24,440 --> 00:22:26,840
which will be conveyed through sophisticated visuals.

269
00:22:28,320 --> 00:22:28,880
Dan.

270
00:22:29,280 --> 00:22:31,680
Why lead the presentation with visuals?

271
00:22:31,680 --> 00:22:33,200
Kimhan is coming back to Thailand.

272
00:22:35,200 --> 00:22:36,120
Why?

273
00:22:36,520 --> 00:22:38,000
Why is he suddenly coming back?

274
00:22:39,120 --> 00:22:42,120
He probably got tired of traveling on his parents’ money.

275
00:22:42,720 --> 00:22:43,480
Dan.

276
00:22:43,720 --> 00:22:46,320
Why lead the presentation with visuals?

277
00:22:50,000 --> 00:22:50,960
Dan?

278
00:22:54,160 --> 00:22:55,040
Uh…

279
00:22:57,720 --> 00:22:58,440
And Saint.

280
00:22:58,840 --> 00:23:01,200
Why include so much numerical detail?

281
00:23:03,520 --> 00:23:04,560
Just a moment, please.

282
00:23:07,280 --> 00:23:08,560
Please look into it.

283
00:23:09,880 --> 00:23:12,120
Tomorrow, we’re meeting the client at HQ.

284
00:23:12,280 --> 00:23:15,160
Every team, have your final sales presentation ready.

285
00:23:15,680 --> 00:23:17,440
Understood.

286
00:23:22,480 --> 00:23:23,320
Ow!

287
00:23:24,000 --> 00:23:24,760
What’s wrong?

288
00:23:28,720 --> 00:23:29,680
I got a cramp.

289
00:23:30,560 --> 00:23:31,440
I’m sorry.

290
00:23:33,040 --> 00:23:35,000
Relax. Don’t tense up.

291
00:23:47,680 --> 00:23:48,320
P’Ta.

292
00:23:48,320 --> 00:23:51,320
We’ve gathered all the information from our meetings

293
00:23:51,440 --> 00:23:56,160
and analyzed the strengths and weaknesses.

294
00:24:07,800 --> 00:24:08,800
Don’t worry.

295
00:24:09,840 --> 00:24:11,080
You can do this.

296
00:24:12,800 --> 00:24:13,920
I believe in you.

297
00:24:17,600 --> 00:24:19,040
Just go in there

298
00:24:20,000 --> 00:24:21,680
and be yourself.

299
00:24:22,440 --> 00:24:23,400
That’s enough.

300
00:24:24,200 --> 00:24:27,000
I’m not afraid of the work,

301
00:24:27,000 --> 00:24:28,920
It’s my past I’m afraid of.

302
00:24:29,680 --> 00:24:30,160
Mm.

303
00:24:30,960 --> 00:24:31,680
Thank you.

304
00:24:32,040 --> 00:24:32,600
Let’s go.

305
00:24:45,360 --> 00:24:46,120
Please have a seat.

306
00:24:48,840 --> 00:24:50,320
Shall we get started?

307
00:24:50,520 --> 00:24:51,440
One moment, please.

308
00:24:51,800 --> 00:24:53,040
We have one more person.

309
00:25:07,400 --> 00:25:09,520
Please welcome our new CEO,

310
00:25:09,520 --> 00:25:10,520
Mr. Kimhan.

311
00:25:10,520 --> 00:25:13,160
He’ll be joining us today.

312
00:25:14,240 --> 00:25:15,000
Hello.

313
00:25:15,600 --> 00:25:16,960
I’ve been looking forward…

314
00:25:17,720 --> 00:25:19,280
to today’s presentation.

315
00:25:19,760 --> 00:25:20,960
I hope you’ll do your best.

316
00:25:21,200 --> 00:25:21,680
Of course.

317
00:26:52,280 --> 00:26:53,920
Let’s get started.

318
00:26:54,840 --> 00:26:57,360
Our analysis of the target audience

319
00:26:57,840 --> 00:26:59,200
shows that

320
00:26:59,200 --> 00:27:00,680
interest in luxury lifestyles

321
00:27:00,680 --> 00:27:03,080
rose by 18% in Q3.

322
00:27:03,480 --> 00:27:05,000
Our key message is

323
00:27:05,320 --> 00:27:06,680
‘Living above the ordinary’,

324
00:27:06,880 --> 00:27:09,000
which will be conveyed through sophisticated visuals.

325
00:27:09,200 --> 00:27:13,720
We’ll shoot at iconic locations in Bangkok,

326
00:27:13,720 --> 00:27:16,120
using fast-paced camera movements

327
00:27:16,160 --> 00:27:18,440
to capture the urban lifestyle.

328
00:27:18,720 --> 00:27:22,560
Our communication strategy will maximize impact

329
00:27:22,560 --> 00:27:26,520
in both brand image and sales.

330
00:27:35,440 --> 00:27:35,840
And...

331
00:27:36,720 --> 00:27:38,120
In Q3,

332
00:27:38,360 --> 00:27:42,120
Siam Central department store saw sales grow 12.7%,

333
00:27:42,160 --> 00:27:45,200
compared to the same period last year.

334
00:27:45,440 --> 00:27:48,320
That’s well above

335
00:27:48,320 --> 00:27:51,920
the retail market average of just 7–8%.

336
00:27:52,560 --> 00:27:56,040
These figures show that the Siam Central campaign

337
00:27:56,160 --> 00:27:58,640
won’t just build brand awareness.

338
00:27:58,800 --> 00:28:01,200
It’ll also drive actual sales.

339
00:28:01,360 --> 00:28:02,960
Because our existing customers

340
00:28:02,960 --> 00:28:06,520
will become early adopters for our brand.

341
00:28:07,680 --> 00:28:10,520
All of this reinforces the idea

342
00:28:10,800 --> 00:28:12,720
that our department store

343
00:28:12,720 --> 00:28:14,800
is a place to experience life.

344
00:28:15,200 --> 00:28:16,960
And that’s why we’re confident

345
00:28:16,960 --> 00:28:19,200
that this campaign

346
00:28:19,720 --> 00:28:22,160
won’t just boost sales.

347
00:28:22,360 --> 00:28:24,120
It’ll also elevate our brand image

348
00:28:24,120 --> 00:28:27,920
as the country’s new hub for luxury lifestyles.

349
00:28:37,280 --> 00:28:38,320
I have a question.

350
00:28:39,920 --> 00:28:41,800
Q3 sales did increase.

351
00:28:43,360 --> 00:28:45,800
But online channels are growing much faster,

352
00:28:46,040 --> 00:28:49,240
Why do you think a luxury mall campaign

353
00:28:49,240 --> 00:28:50,520
can make a bigger impact

354
00:28:50,520 --> 00:28:52,120
than online media buying?

355
00:28:56,320 --> 00:28:57,080
Well…

356
00:29:06,800 --> 00:29:07,680
That’s a fair point.

357
00:29:10,240 --> 00:29:12,080
Let me answer your question, Mr. Kimhan.

358
00:29:14,160 --> 00:29:15,600
Online channels are growing fast,

359
00:29:15,600 --> 00:29:17,160
but if we look deeper,

360
00:29:17,160 --> 00:29:18,920
Siam Central’s customers

361
00:29:18,920 --> 00:29:21,160
are willing to pay for premium experiences.

362
00:29:22,160 --> 00:29:24,160
They’re not just looking at online reviews.

363
00:29:24,160 --> 00:29:25,800
They want an experience.

364
00:29:26,360 --> 00:29:28,560
They want to immerse themselves in luxury

365
00:29:28,560 --> 00:29:30,640
that fits their lifestyle.

366
00:29:30,800 --> 00:29:33,040
That’s something online shopping can’t replicate.

367
00:29:33,400 --> 00:29:35,600
The Q3 traffic figures

368
00:29:35,600 --> 00:29:38,840
showing a 20% increase are interesting.

369
00:29:40,880 --> 00:29:42,680
But how can you be sure

370
00:29:42,680 --> 00:29:44,320
that this increase in foot traffic

371
00:29:44,720 --> 00:29:46,440
will translate into actual sales,

372
00:29:47,120 --> 00:29:49,240
rather than people just browsing and leaving?

373
00:29:49,400 --> 00:29:50,040
That’s right.

374
00:29:50,880 --> 00:29:53,560
Traffic doesn’t guarantee sales.

375
00:29:54,840 --> 00:29:56,280
Most of that 20% growth

376
00:29:56,280 --> 00:29:58,760
comes from the high-spending segment,

377
00:29:58,760 --> 00:30:01,080
who are ready to buy,

378
00:30:01,080 --> 00:30:02,200
not just to window-shop.

379
00:30:02,200 --> 00:30:05,280
The mall’s data also shows that spending per head

380
00:30:05,280 --> 00:30:07,800
is almost twice the market average.

381
00:30:08,160 --> 00:30:10,520
If we offer products worthy of that setting,

382
00:30:10,960 --> 00:30:12,720
we’re not just selling products,

383
00:30:12,720 --> 00:30:14,320
but we’re selling a feeling.

384
00:30:14,720 --> 00:30:17,960
The feeling of living above the ordinary.

385
00:30:17,960 --> 00:30:19,280
And that feeling

386
00:30:19,280 --> 00:30:21,560
will turn foot traffic into actual customers.

387
00:30:28,280 --> 00:30:29,320
Excellent.

388
00:30:30,160 --> 00:30:32,560
That’s what they want to hear.

389
00:30:33,160 --> 00:30:34,240
Thank you.

390
00:30:51,400 --> 00:30:53,280
Alright. That's all for today.

391
00:30:53,800 --> 00:30:56,000
If you have any questions, come see me next week.

392
00:30:56,000 --> 00:30:56,880
Class dismissed.

393
00:31:07,600 --> 00:31:09,000
Professor.

394
00:31:09,320 --> 00:31:11,560
Thank you so much for today’s class.

395
00:31:11,560 --> 00:31:12,560
I really enjoyed it.

396
00:31:13,320 --> 00:31:16,400
I’ll ask you more about the assignment next week.

397
00:31:16,840 --> 00:31:18,600
Of course. See you then.

398
00:31:18,800 --> 00:31:20,520
-Goodbye.
-Goodbye.

399
00:31:30,320 --> 00:31:32,120
(What are you doing?)

400
00:31:37,000 --> 00:31:38,360
(What are you planning now?)

401
00:31:47,600 --> 00:31:48,840
(You’ll find out soon.)

402
00:32:09,840 --> 00:32:10,560
P’Ta.

403
00:32:10,880 --> 00:32:12,600
The new CEO is so intense.

404
00:32:12,960 --> 00:32:16,320
I thought we were all doomed!

405
00:32:16,600 --> 00:32:17,600
I was shrinking.

406
00:32:17,600 --> 00:32:19,080
So tense.

407
00:32:19,280 --> 00:32:20,920
Really tense.

408
00:32:23,400 --> 00:32:25,000
I thought I wouldn’t make it either.

409
00:32:26,680 --> 00:32:28,880
Everyone did a great job.

410
00:32:28,880 --> 00:32:29,800
Especially Saint.

411
00:32:30,600 --> 00:32:32,480
Your answers were spot-on.

412
00:32:32,480 --> 00:32:34,200
They were really impressed.

413
00:32:34,200 --> 00:32:35,800
-Thank you.
-Our team’s amazing.

414
00:32:36,080 --> 00:32:38,320
-Fantastic.
-Good job, everyone.

415
00:32:46,360 --> 00:32:46,880
Dan.

416
00:32:49,680 --> 00:32:50,800
You did really well.

417
00:32:53,120 --> 00:32:53,560
Mm.

418
00:32:54,680 --> 00:32:56,560
I guess I did.

419
00:33:03,400 --> 00:33:04,800
Is Mr. Kimhan…

420
00:33:07,520 --> 00:33:08,800
what’s bothering you?

421
00:33:10,320 --> 00:33:10,920
No.

422
00:33:11,600 --> 00:33:12,600
I’m just a little tired.

423
00:33:13,800 --> 00:33:14,920
I’m gonna take a break.

424
00:33:15,720 --> 00:33:16,840
Need a ride?

425
00:33:20,160 --> 00:33:21,640
I noticed you didn’t drive today.

426
00:33:21,880 --> 00:33:22,720
It’s okay.

427
00:33:23,520 --> 00:33:24,480
I can get home on my own.

428
00:33:42,160 --> 00:33:43,520
The rain falling

429
00:33:45,000 --> 00:33:47,960
is nothing compared to the weight on my heart.

430
00:34:26,760 --> 00:34:28,480
Let me walk you to the station.

431
00:34:30,600 --> 00:34:32,080
so you don’t get wet.

432
00:34:37,080 --> 00:34:37,800
It’s okay.

433
00:34:39,400 --> 00:34:40,639
I want to go alone.

434
00:35:26,240 --> 00:35:27,320
Why are you so soaked?

435
00:35:41,400 --> 00:35:42,200
P’James.

436
00:35:46,200 --> 00:35:47,760
Do you know?

437
00:35:50,160 --> 00:35:52,560
The client for the major project I’m working on

438
00:35:55,800 --> 00:35:56,680
is…

439
00:35:57,680 --> 00:35:58,800
P’Kimhan.

440
00:36:03,880 --> 00:36:05,360
I don’t want him to come back.

441
00:36:10,280 --> 00:36:11,000
P’James.

442
00:36:16,960 --> 00:36:18,280
I like you.

443
00:36:19,680 --> 00:36:21,960
I’ve liked you since we first met.

444
00:36:24,960 --> 00:36:25,640
Hey!

445
00:36:26,400 --> 00:36:27,840
Watch where you’re going!

446
00:36:28,000 --> 00:36:28,920
I’m sorry.

447
00:36:29,200 --> 00:36:30,120
I didn’t mean to.

448
00:36:30,800 --> 00:36:31,840
Looking for trouble?

449
00:36:41,840 --> 00:36:43,600
You bumped into him first.

450
00:36:58,480 --> 00:37:01,400
You may not even remember when we first met.

451
00:37:02,200 --> 00:37:04,400
But I’ve always remembered.

452
00:37:07,120 --> 00:37:09,040
I’ve held on to that feeling

453
00:37:09,320 --> 00:37:12,520
and kept it a secret for over ten years.

454
00:37:15,200 --> 00:37:16,040
Dan.

455
00:37:21,640 --> 00:37:23,200
Thank you so much

456
00:37:25,360 --> 00:37:27,600
for telling me how you feel.

457
00:37:32,320 --> 00:37:33,520
I’m really glad

458
00:37:35,960 --> 00:37:37,560
to have you in my life.

459
00:37:39,760 --> 00:37:41,720
You mean a lot to me.

460
00:37:43,800 --> 00:37:45,680
I trust you

461
00:37:48,800 --> 00:37:50,640
and feel comfortable with you.

462
00:37:54,480 --> 00:37:55,960
But don’t you think...

463
00:38:01,960 --> 00:38:03,280
we’re better off

464
00:38:04,280 --> 00:38:05,560
just the way we are?

465
00:38:15,440 --> 00:38:17,120
Better off like this?

466
00:38:22,560 --> 00:38:24,160
What’s so good about it?

467
00:38:25,800 --> 00:38:27,600
I have to keep these feelings to myself.

468
00:38:27,880 --> 00:38:28,960
Keep them a secret.

469
00:38:30,160 --> 00:38:31,520
I can’t tell anyone.

470
00:38:32,240 --> 00:38:34,280
I can’t even tell you.

471
00:38:35,760 --> 00:38:37,880
I have to keep smiling as if there’s nothing,

472
00:38:39,480 --> 00:38:41,160
even though deep down,

473
00:38:41,720 --> 00:38:43,800
all I want is to tell you I love you.

474
00:38:44,040 --> 00:38:46,320
Please don’t make this any harder, Dan.

475
00:38:51,440 --> 00:38:52,960
I don’t want to lose you.

476
00:38:56,560 --> 00:38:58,920
I think if we cross that line,

477
00:39:00,680 --> 00:39:02,000
everything will fall apart.

478
00:39:03,400 --> 00:39:06,680
I’m not afraid of things falling apart.

479
00:39:08,160 --> 00:39:09,360
What I’m afraid of

480
00:39:10,480 --> 00:39:12,520
is not being able to stay by your side.

481
00:39:15,920 --> 00:39:17,080
Do you know...

482
00:39:17,640 --> 00:39:20,920
I’ve kept these words for ten years?

483
00:39:23,920 --> 00:39:25,120
And now,

484
00:39:27,600 --> 00:39:30,760
you’re telling me there’s no chance for us?

485
00:39:42,440 --> 00:39:44,080
I want you to be happy, Dan.

486
00:39:48,320 --> 00:39:51,080
But I can’t be the reason for it.

487
00:41:00,920 --> 00:41:02,040
Why are you here?

488
00:41:03,520 --> 00:41:04,640
If it’s not about work,

489
00:41:05,400 --> 00:41:06,680
don’t come to see me again.

490
00:41:08,760 --> 00:41:10,200
Shut up.

491
00:41:13,680 --> 00:41:15,440
I’m not your plaything anymore.

492
00:41:16,040 --> 00:41:17,520
If you have nothing else to say,

493
00:41:17,520 --> 00:41:18,600
I’m leaving.

494
00:41:18,760 --> 00:41:20,400
James.

495
00:41:26,320 --> 00:41:27,240
How’s it going?

496
00:41:27,360 --> 00:41:28,520
I’m exhausted.

497
00:41:29,840 --> 00:41:30,760
Your shirt’s wrinkled.

498
00:41:30,760 --> 00:41:31,680
Did you sleep in it?

499
00:41:31,680 --> 00:41:32,640
No.

500
00:41:32,640 --> 00:41:35,160
I ironed it already.

501
00:41:35,160 --> 00:41:36,360
Really?

502
00:41:36,360 --> 00:41:37,000
Mm.

503
00:41:40,000 --> 00:41:40,920
Can you stop?

504
00:41:43,440 --> 00:41:44,080
Why?

505
00:41:44,880 --> 00:41:46,560
Why is it always like this?

506
00:41:47,400 --> 00:41:48,400
Because...

507
00:41:51,280 --> 00:41:53,240
you can’t say no to me, can you?

508
00:41:55,720 --> 00:41:57,120
Stay away from P’James.

509
00:41:59,120 --> 00:42:00,440
And what do I get in return...

510
00:42:01,480 --> 00:42:03,080
if i do that?

511
00:42:08,480 --> 00:42:09,400
Everything.

512
00:42:11,000 --> 00:42:12,400
Everything you want.

513
00:42:13,680 --> 00:42:14,560
Like today.

514
00:42:15,280 --> 00:42:16,680
You wanted me to come here,

515
00:42:17,680 --> 00:42:18,680
so I did.

516
00:42:21,600 --> 00:42:22,160
Good.

517
00:42:23,800 --> 00:42:24,880
At least,

518
00:42:26,560 --> 00:42:28,000
now you know

519
00:42:28,000 --> 00:42:29,520
you can’t escape me.

520
00:43:09,880 --> 00:43:11,360
Where’s Dan?

521
00:43:14,200 --> 00:43:15,400
No idea.

522
00:43:15,640 --> 00:43:17,120
I haven’t seen him all morning.

523
00:43:19,640 --> 00:43:22,400
Maybe he’s secretly gone on a date.

524
00:43:23,320 --> 00:43:24,360
I doubt it.

525
00:43:24,360 --> 00:43:25,120
Ellie.

526
00:43:25,840 --> 00:43:26,120
Yes.

527
00:43:26,720 --> 00:43:29,040
Everyone, Dan called in sick today.

528
00:43:31,120 --> 00:43:31,640
Okay.

529
00:43:32,760 --> 00:43:34,320
Oh.

530
00:43:34,720 --> 00:43:35,840
Sick leave.

531
00:43:36,000 --> 00:43:37,640
I thought he’d snuck off on a date.

532
00:43:39,120 --> 00:43:40,040
Kinda sus.

533
00:43:40,440 --> 00:43:40,920
Right?

534
00:44:13,600 --> 00:44:13,880
Oh.

535
00:44:17,280 --> 00:44:17,920
That was quick.

536
00:44:48,280 --> 00:44:50,680
What I feared most had come back.

537
00:44:51,560 --> 00:44:52,640
P’Kimhan,

538
00:44:53,320 --> 00:44:55,880
the man who holds all my secrets.

539
00:44:57,160 --> 00:44:58,680
I’m not your plaything anymore.

540
00:44:58,680 --> 00:45:00,320
James.

541
00:45:01,320 --> 00:45:02,440
Stop,

542
00:45:02,440 --> 00:45:03,880
or I’ll expose your secret.

543
00:45:04,680 --> 00:45:06,520
Then I’ll expose yours first.

544
00:45:09,400 --> 00:45:11,080
Can I be someone you trust?

545
00:45:11,080 --> 00:45:13,560
Maybe I’m not who you think I am.

546
00:45:13,840 --> 00:45:15,680
He can afford designer brands

547
00:45:15,880 --> 00:45:17,360
because he’s a sugar baby!

548
00:45:17,360 --> 00:45:18,120
Whoa.

549
00:45:19,560 --> 00:45:20,920
Saint!

550
00:45:20,920 --> 00:45:21,520
Please stop!

551
00:45:21,520 --> 00:45:23,440
Keep this asshole out of our business!
